  "summary": "EFF's membership-drive post celebrates its legal defense of DeFlock.me creator Will Freeman against trademark-based cease-and-desist threats from Flock Safety, and frames growing local pushback against ALPR contracts as a movement EFF supports. The piece solicits donations and promotes related EFF reporting on Flock surveillance.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Will created the website DeFlock.me to reveal the dangers of automated license plate readers (ALPRs)\u2014cameras that collect location data on every vehicle they see and upload that to a massive nationwide police database.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "when the police spy-tech company Flock Safety went after Will's website with legal threats citing trademark law, he saw it for what it was: an attempt to silence critics",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "In cities around the country, privacy advocates are pressuring officials to block or end contracts for ALPRs\u2014and winning.",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    }
  ],
